# Commit-identity map. Git, `git shortlog`, `git blame`, `git log --use-mailmap` and
# every forge read this file, so a published commit is *shown* under the identity the
# team now uses without the object being rewritten.
#
# The entry below covers 21 commits published before the role-mailbox rule took
# effect (boundary: LEGACY_IDENTITY_BEFORE in src/teamwork/engine.py). Published
# history is protected and rewriting it is a red line, so the bytes stay in the
# objects; this file is what stops a personal name and address being displayed, and
# `tests/unit/test_mailmap.py` fails when a commit appears that neither carries a
# role mailbox nor is mapped here.
#
#   <proper identity>              <committed identity>
CEO <ceo@agents.nidvue.com>       <<redacted-personal-email>>
